title: 1872 Republican National Convention
subtitle: Republican Candidate for President
tags: event
view-if: year = 1872 and month = 5
max-visits: 1

= Republican National Convention, 1872

[? if president = "Grant" : President Grant seeks a second term. With the prestige of the presidency behind him, no serious challenger has emerged from within the party. The nomination is his if he wants it. ?]

[? if president = "Wade" : President Wade's **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">radical</span>** tenure has energized the base but alarmed **<span style="color: #B5651D;">conservatives</span>** and **<span style="color: #9D2933;">moderates</span>** alike. Several challengers have emerged, sensing an opportunity to steer the party in a different direction. ?]

[? if president = "Chase" : President Chase's **<span style="color: #9D2933;">moderate</span>** presidency has frustrated the **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical Wing</span>**. His handling of Reconstruction has drawn criticism from both flanks, and challengers are lining up. ?]

- @Grant_renominate: Ulysses S. Grant
- @Wade_defend: Defend Wade's nomination
- @Chase_defend: Defend Chase's nomination
- @Reno_challenge_Wade: Support a challenger against Wade
- @Reno_challenge_Chase: Support a challenger against Chase

@Grant_renominate
title: Renominate President Grant
view-if: president = "Grant"
on-arrival: {!
    Q.Candidate = "Grant";
    Q.radical_dissent += 2;
    Q.moderate_dissent -= 3;
    Q.conservative_dissent -= 3;
    Q.liberal_dissent += 5;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 2;
    Q.rural_rep += 1;
    Q.workers_rep += 1;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Ulysses_S._Grant_1870-1880.jpg
go-to: VP_1872

Grant is unanimously renominated. The party rallies around the incumbent president, presenting a united front going into the general election. The <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> are dissatisfied with Grant and there dissent increases.

@Wade_defend
title: Back Wade for renomination
view-if: president = "Wade"
choose-if: radical_strength >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** faction is not strong enough to hold off the challengers.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.Candidate = "Wade";
    Q.radical_dissent -= 5;
    Q.radical_strength += 4;
    Q.moderate_dissent += 6;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 8;
    Q.liberal_dissent += 10;
    Q.freemen_rep += 3;
    Q.workers_rep += 2;
    Q.middle_class_rep -= 2;
    Q.rural_rep -= 1;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Benjamin_F_Wade.jpg
go-to: VP_1872

After a bruising floor fight, Wade secures renomination. The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** wing is triumphant, but the convention has left deep scars. **<span style="color: #B5651D;">Conservative</span>** and **<span style="color: #9D2933;">moderate</span>** delegates walk out muttering about bolt candidates. The <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> dissent continues to increase.

@Chase_defend
title: Back Chase for renomination
view-if: president = "Chase"
choose-if: moderate_strength + conservative_strength >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: The **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate</span>** and **<span style="color: #B5651D;">Conservative</span>** factions are too weak to hold the nomination.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.Candidate = "Chase";
    Q.moderate_dissent -= 3;
    Q.conservative_dissent -= 3;
    Q.radical_dissent += 8;
    Q.liberal_dissent -= 2;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 3;
    Q.rural_rep += 2;
    Q.freemen_rep -= 3;
    Q.workers_rep -= 1;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Salmon-P-Chase.webp
go-to: VP_1872

Chase is renominated over **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** objections. The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** wing is furious several prominent members publicly refuse to campaign for him. The <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span>, who had flirted with running their own candidate, are somewhat mollified but not fully satisfied.

@Reno_challenge_Wade
title: Support a challenger to unseat Wade
view-if: president = "Wade"
on-arrival: {!

    // Challenger succeeds based on moderate + conservative + liberal strength vs radical
    let challengerStrength = (Q.moderate_strength || 0) + (Q.conservative_strength || 0) + (Q.liberal_strength || 0);
    let wadeStrength = (Q.radical_strength || 0) + 20; // incumbency bonus

    if (challengerStrength > wadeStrength) {
        if ((Q.conservative_strength || 0) >= (Q.moderate_strength || 0)) {
            Q.Candidate = "Conkling";
        } else {
            Q.Candidate = "Blaine";
        }
        Q.radical_dissent += 15;
        Q.radical_strength -= 5;
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 5;
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 5;
        Q.liberal_dissent -= 3;
        Q.middle_class_rep += 4;
        Q.rural_rep += 3;
        Q.freemen_rep -= 5;
        Q.workers_rep -= 2;
        Q.challenger_beat_wade = 1;
    } else {
        // Challenge fails, Wade holds
        Q.Candidate = "Wade";
        Q.radical_strength += 3;
        Q.radical_dissent -= 3;
        Q.moderate_dissent += 5;
        Q.conservative_dissent += 5;
        Q.liberal_dissent += 8;
        Q.challenger_beat_wade = 0;
    }
!}
go-to: challenger_wade_result

@challenger_wade_result
go-to: VP_1872 if challenger_beat_wade = 1; wade_holds if challenger_beat_wade = 0

@wade_holds
face-image: img/portraits/Benjamin_F_Wade.jpg

The challenge fails. Despite fierce opposition from **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderates</span>** and **<span style="color: #B5651D;">Conservatives</span>**, Wade's **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** base holds firm on the convention floor. Wade is renominated, though the battle has wounded the party.

- @VP_1872: Proceed to the Vice Presidential nomination.

@challenger_wade_result_win
view-if: Candidate = "Conkling" or Candidate = "Blaine"
go-to: VP_1872

[? if Candidate = "Conkling" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/Roscoe_Conkling.jpg" alt="Roscoe Conkling" class="face-img"></div> ?][? if Candidate = "Blaine" : <div class="face-figure"><img src="img/portraits/James_G._Blaine.jpg" alt="James Blaine" class="face-img"></div> ?]

[? if Candidate = "Conkling" : Roscoe Conkling of New York, backed by the **<span style="color: #B5651D;">conservative</span>** machine, defeats Wade on the convention floor. The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radicals</span>** are incandescent with rage. ?][? if Candidate = "Blaine" : James Blaine of Maine, the **<span style="color: #9D2933;">moderate</span>** favorite, outmaneuvers Wade's forces and secures the nomination. The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radicals</span>** feel betrayed. ?]

@Reno_challenge_Chase
title: Support a challenger to unseat Chase
view-if: president = "Chase"
on-arrival: {!

    let challengerStrength = (Q.radical_strength || 0) + (Q.liberal_strength || 0);
    let chaseStrength = (Q.moderate_strength || 0) + (Q.conservative_strength || 0) + 20;

    if (challengerStrength > chaseStrength) {
        Q.Candidate = "Grant";
        Q.radical_dissent -= 5;
        Q.radical_strength += 4;
        Q.moderate_dissent += 8;
        Q.conservative_dissent += 6;
        Q.liberal_dissent += 5;
        Q.freemen_rep += 4;
        Q.workers_rep += 2;
        Q.middle_class_rep -= 2;
        Q.challenger_beat_chase = 1;
    } else {
        Q.Candidate = "Chase";
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 3;
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 3;
        Q.radical_dissent += 8;
        Q.challenger_beat_chase = 0;
    }
!}
go-to: challenger_chase_result

@challenger_chase_result
go-to: VP_1872 if challenger_beat_chase = 1; chase_holds if challenger_beat_chase = 0

@chase_holds
face-image: img/portraits/Salmon-P-Chase.webp

Chase's **<span style="color: #9D2933;">moderate</span>** and **<span style="color: #B5651D;">conservative</span>** coalition holds on the convention floor. The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radicals</span>** challenge is beaten back, though the bitterness will linger through the campaign.

- @VP_1872: Proceed to the Vice Presidential nomination.

@VP_1872

= Vice Presidential Nomination

With the presidential nominee chosen, the convention turns to the question of the Vice Presidency. The right running mate can balance the ticket and shore up wavering factions.

Our candidate is **[+ Candidate +]**.

- @Wilson_VP: Henry Wilson (Massachusetts)
- @Colfax_VP: Schuyler Colfax (Indiana)
- @Maynard_VP: Horace Maynard (Tennessee)
- @Davis_VP: David Davis (Illinois)

@Wilson_VP
subtitle: **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical Republican</span>**. Strong labor ties and abolitionist credentials.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.VPCandidate = "Wilson";
    Q.radical_dissent -= 4;
    Q.radical_strength += 3;
    Q.moderate_dissent += 2;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 3;
    Q.workers_rep += 4;
    Q.freemen_rep += 3;
    Q.immigrant_laborers_rep += 2;
    Q.middle_class_rep -= 1;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Henry_Wilson,_VP_of_the_United_States.jpg
go-to: convention_end_1872

Henry Wilson, the "Natick Cobbler," brings strong **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** and labor credentials to the ticket. A former shoemaker turned senator, his working-class origins appeal to Northern industrial workers. He is deeply committed to Black civil rights, which energizes the freedmen vote but alarms **<span style="color: #B5651D;">conservatives</span>**.

@Colfax_VP
subtitle: **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate</span>**. Popular Speaker of the House, broadly acceptable to the party.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.VPCandidate = "Colfax";
    Q.moderate_strength += 3;
    Q.moderate_dissent -= 3;
    Q.conservative_dissent -= 2;
    Q.radical_dissent += 2;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 3;
    Q.rural_rep += 2;
    Q.workers_rep += 1;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Schuyler_Colfax,_photo_portrait_seated,_c1855-1865.jpg
go-to: convention_end_1872

Schuyler Colfax, the affable Speaker of the House, is a safe and familiar choice. His **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate</span>** Republicanism and broad name recognition make him acceptable to most factions. The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radicals</span>** are not thrilled, but they will campaign for the ticket.

@Maynard_VP
subtitle: <span style="color: #B22222;">**Southern Unionist**</span>. Could help carry border states and signal reconciliation.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.VPCandidate = "Maynard";
    Q.conservative_strength += 4;
    Q.conservative_dissent -= 3;
    Q.liberal_strength += 2;
    Q.radical_dissent += 6;
    Q.rural_rep += 4;
    Q.freemen_rep -= 3;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 2;
    Q.TN_rural_rep += 5;
    Q.KY_rural_rep += 3;
    Q.WV_rural_rep += 3;
!}
go-to: convention_end_1872
face-image: img/portraits/Horace_Maynard_-_Brady-Handy.jpg

Horace Maynard of Tennessee is a <span style="color: #B22222;">**Southern Unionist**</span> whose nomination signals the party's desire to build a broader coalition in the upper South. His selection pleases **<span style="color: #B5651D;">conservatives</span>** and border-state <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span>, but **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radicals</span>** deeply distrust any overture toward Southern reconciliation.

@Davis_VP
subtitle: Independent. Lincoln's former campaign manager, pragmatic and broadly trusted.
choose-if: moderate_strength >= 25
unavailable-subtitle: The **<span style="color: #9D2933;">moderate</span>** faction is too weak to push Davis onto the ticket.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.VPCandidate = "Davis";
    Q.moderate_strength += 5;
    Q.liberal_strength += 3;
    Q.conservative_dissent -= 2;
    Q.radical_dissent += 4;
    Q.liberal_dissent -= 4;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 4;
    Q.rural_rep += 2;
    Q.workers_rep += 1;
    Q.freemen_rep -= 1;
!}
go-to: convention_end_1872
face-image: img/portraits/960px-David_Davis_Supreme_Court_justice_-_Brady-Handy

David Davis, Lincoln's old friend and former campaign manager, brings a pragmatic independence that appeals to **<span style="color: #9D2933;">moderates</span>** and **<span style="color: #DAA520;">liberals</span>**. He is not a doctrinaire **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>**, and his selection is seen as a gesture toward the <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> dissidents. The **<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">Radical</span>** wing is displeased but not mutinous.

@convention_end_1872

= The Ticket is Set

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican Party**</span> will enter the 1872 election with **[+ Candidate +]** for President and **[+ VPCandidate +]** for Vice President.

[? if liberal_dissent >= 25 : The <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> faction is threatening to bolt and run their own candidate. If they do, the anti-<span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democrat**</span> vote will be split. ?]

[? if radical_dissent >= 25 : <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> are openly grumbling about the ticket. Their enthusiasm or lack of it could suppress turnout among freedmen and Northern reformers. ?]

[? if liberal_dissent < 25 and radical_dissent < 25 : The party appears broadly unified behind the ticket. ?]